      "content": "The supposed labor protections within the TPP were often weak and easily circumvented by corporate lobbying. While some provisions mentioned labor standards, they were largely toothless compared to the economic power of the signatory nations. In practice, the agreement's focus on free trade meant that any labor gains were overshadowed by the drive for cheaper production, which ultimately suppressed wages for the average worker. The narrative of worker protection was a political talking point, not a functional reality of the deal.",
